      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need some help writing a rejection email. i have a candidate who made it all the way to the final round for a software engineer role but we ended up going with someone else. i want to be polite and empathetic so we don't burn the bridge, but keep it professional. can u give me a template?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a template for your rejection email, focusing on politeness and professionalism. I've made sure it's kind, even though the news is tough to deliver.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Update on the Software Engineer Position at [Company Name]**\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nThank you so much for taking the time to interview with us for the Software Engineer role. We truly enjoyed getting to know you and learning more about your skills and experience during the final round. The caliber of candidates was incredibly high, which made our decision very difficult.\n\nWe have decided to move forward with another candidate whose specific background was a slightly closer match to the immediate needs of this particular role. Please know this decision was not a reflection of your abilities, as we were very impressed with [mention something specific, e.g., your problem-solving approach or technical depth].\n\nWe sincerely appreciate your interest in [Company Name] and wish you the very best in your job search and future endeavors. We hope you'll keep us in mind for future opportunities that might be a better fit.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name]\n\n***\n\nRemember to personalize the bracketed sections, especially the specific compliment, to make it feel genuine",
