    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks this is good. can u make it sound a bit more personal tho? like slightly more warm and less like a generic automated response? i want them to feel like we actually liked them even though they didnt get it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To make it warmer, you need to inject a bit more genuine appreciation into the language. You can shift the tone from formal assessment to sincere recognition of their effort.\n\nHere is a revised template that feels more personal and warm. It still maintains professionalism, but it sounds like a human reaching out, not a script being read.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Following Up on the Software Engineer Role at [Company Name]**\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to reach out personally regarding the Software Engineer position. We were genuinely impressed throughout the entire interview process, and I especially enjoyed our conversations about [mention a specific project or topic they discussed]. It was a pleasure getting to know you.\n\nThis was a truly difficult decision because the final round was so competitive. We ultimately decided to move forward with a candidate whose experience aligned slightly more closely with the immediate demands of this specific team structure right now.\n\nPlease know that this was a tough call, and it does not diminish how highly we regard your talent. We truly appreciate the time and energy you invested in meeting with us. I hope our paths cross again, and I encourage you to keep an eye on our careers page for future openings.\n\nWishing you the very best in finding a",
